A||||3||Bautsch||Battery Light???
Z||000000||Bautsch||09-02-99||06:41 PM||||My battery light came on today and I'm not sure why. My battery was bad and I replaced it but the light is still on. I had the altenator tested and it tested ok. Any suggestions?<p>Thanks,<br>Mike Bautsch<br>mike@macvend.com
Z||000001||batboy||09-02-99||07:24 PM||||Usually, the alternator is not charging properly when the "battery light" comes on.
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-02-99||09:21 PM||||This may be an insulting comment due to its simplicity, but did you replace/examine the battery cables.  If they are full of corrosion, it will be difficult for the alternator to efficiently charge the battery due to the increased resistance.
Z||000003||Speadraser||09-03-99||10:02 AM||||Be sure the two wires in the connector are not cut or damaged.  I had a problem with mine because the wires are real close to the RH driveshaft.  The driveshaft wore the wire in two.  Fixed the wire and the light went out.  There is also a diode that is wired in the wiring harness on the computer side of the bulkhead connector.  This I believe can also cause this problem.  I don't know the exact spec of the diode or if its readable off of it, but if thats your problem and you replace it you must observe its polarity.  Hope this helps.<br>Speady
